course: dictionary
lesson: 8672
title: Secure: safe and firmly fixed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Secure is a word with several meanings. The clues in the sentence tell you which one the author means. «A smart home has lights, heating and locks connected to the internet that can be controlled by phone or voice, and a smart thermostat can learn when people are home; the accounts must be kept secure.» The accounts must be protected from people who should not get in, so secure means safe from harm.
explain: Secure can also describe something that is firmly fixed. A secure lock or a secure load on a trailer will not move or fall. When you see secure, ask: is this about safety, about something fixed in place, or about a feeling? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Secure is also a verb, so it has forms: secure, secures, secured, securing. To secure something means to fix it firmly or to lock it. «Use 4 nails to secure each board» tells you the nails hold each board firmly in place.
fact: Secure means safe, protected from danger or harm.
fact: Secure means firmly fixed, so it will not move or fall.
fact: To secure something is to fix it firmly or to lock it.
fact: Feeling secure means feeling safe and not worried.
fact: «The accounts must be kept secure» means they must be protected from people who should not get in.
exercise: «The accounts must be kept secure.» What does secure mean here? | Loose and wobbly | *Safe, so that people who should not get in cannot | Pretty and decorated | Left open for everyone
exercise: Dad says, «Use 4 nails to secure each board.» What does secure mean here? | To paint the board | *To fix it firmly so it will not move | To sell it at the shop | To measure the length of the board
exercise: Which word means feeling safe and not worried? | Anxious | Nervous | Worried | *Secure
test: Feeling secure means | feeling cold and wet | feeling lost in a new place | *feeling safe and not worried
test: A secure website is one that is | open to anyone who wants to look | very slow to load | *protected so others cannot take your details
exam: Which sentence uses secure to mean firmly fixed? | I feel secure when my family is near | *Use screws to secure the shelf to the wall | The shelf was secure with a screw, so I felt safe | My secure friend lives next door
